First, the problem is that when you pass an object as `options.values` into `new Field(...)`, the Field constructor and its `setValues`/`setValue` routines directly mutate that very same object. In other words:

1. In the constructor you do  
   ```js
   this.values = options.values || {};
   ```
   so `this.values` *is* the original object.
2. Later on, every time you call `setValue` or `setValues`, you write directly into `this.values`, which writes back into the user’s object.

What you want instead is to make a fresh copy of the user’s data at construction time, and only ever mutate that copy internally.

